{% comment %}
  Rebrand header — logo lockup left, two path pills and a burger right, on
  white. Comp: 1920 x 170, pills 61px tall, burger 48px wide.

  The comp shows no cart or search in the bar, so those are off by default and
  the cart lives in the drawer instead; a store still needs a route to it.
  Turn the header icons on if the client wants them in the bar.
{% endcomment %}

{{ 'saf-rebrand.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
<script src="{{ 'saf-rebrand.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

{%- liquid
  assign sid = section.id
  assign menu = section.settings.menu

  comment
    Optional dropdowns under the two path buttons, for the variant Bianca is
    being shown. A section may only carry ONE link_list setting, so the two
    menus arrive as blocks instead — the same workaround the pre-rebrand header
    used.

    The button itself stays a link. The old site had a label that only opened a
    menu and went nowhere; that dead end is the thing being fixed, not
    repeated.
  endcomment
  assign drop_a = ''
  assign drop_b = ''
  for block in section.blocks
    if block.type == 'path_menu'
      if block.settings.which == 'b'
        assign drop_b = block.settings.menu
      else
        assign drop_a = block.settings.menu
      endif
    endif
  endfor

  assign has_drop_a = false
  assign has_drop_b = false
  if section.settings.enable_dropdowns
    if linklists[drop_a].links.size > 0
      assign has_drop_a = true
    endif
    if linklists[drop_b].links.size > 0
      assign has_drop_b = true
    endif
  endif
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  Which side of the site are we on? Drives the `is-here` pill state below.
  A snippet's assigns do not escape `render`, so capture the echo.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture rb_active -%}
  {%- render 'rb-active-path',
    a_url: section.settings.cta_a_url,
    b_url: section.settings.cta_b_url,
    a_paths: section.settings.cta_a_paths,
    b_paths: section.settings.cta_b_paths
  -%}
{%- endcapture -%}
{%- liquid
  assign rb_active = rb_active | strip
  unless section.settings.highlight_active
    assign rb_active = ''
  endunless
  assign cls_a = 'rb-btn rb-btn--plain rb-btn--' | append: section.settings.cta_a_fill
  assign cls_b = 'rb-btn rb-btn--plain rb-btn--' | append: section.settings.cta_b_fill
  comment
    Both pills are solid in the comp, so "here" cannot be signalled by adding
    colour — the colour IS each side's identity. Mark it by STEPPING THE OTHER
    ONE BACK instead: the side you are on keeps its fill, the side you are not
    on drops to an outline of its own colour. On home/cart/search neither
    matches and the pair stays exactly as Hanre drew it.
  endcomment
  if rb_active == 'a'
    assign cls_a = cls_a | append: ' is-here is-here--a'
    assign cls_b = cls_b | append: ' is-away is-away--b'
  elsif rb_active == 'b'
    assign cls_b = cls_b | append: ' is-here is-here--b'
    assign cls_a = cls_a | append: ' is-away is-away--a'
  endif
-%}

<style>
  /* The sticky header is its own stacking context, so the drawer's z-index is
     only relative to THIS value — not to the page. It has to clear the
     floating WhatsApp button (55) and the legacy mobile bar (60), while
     staying under the lead/newsletter popups (9999+). */
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 70;
  }
  {%- if section.settings.sticky -%}
    #shopify-section-{{ sid }} { position: sticky; top: 0; }
  {%- endif -%}

  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-header {
    background: {{ section.settings.background }};
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 16px;
    min-height: var(--rb-header-h);
    padding-inline: clamp(16px, 3.65vw, 70px);
    {% if section.settings.show_border %}border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(30, 30, 30, 0.12);{% endif %}
  }
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-header__logo { display: block; flex: 0 0 auto; }
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-header__logo img {
    display: block;
    width: {{ section.settings.logo_width }}px;
    max-width: 46vw;
    height: auto;
  }
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-header__right {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: clamp(10px, 1.41vw, 27px);
  }
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-header__icon {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 44px;
    height: 44px;
    color: {{ section.settings.text_color }};
    text-decoration: none;
    position: relative;
  }
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-header__icon svg { width: 22px; height: 22px; }
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-header__icon:hover { color: {{ section.settings.icon_hover_color }}; }

  /* "You are here" on the two path pills.
     The side you are on keeps a solid fill in its own colour (moss for Buy
     Art, cherry for Make Art — the same split the home page's two-path panels
     teach). The side you are NOT on steps back to an outline of that same
     colour, so the pair still reads as two colour-coded routes but only one
     of them is lit. Colour alone could not carry this: with both pills solid
     the "here" fill and the resting fill are the same hex. */
  .rb-btn.is-here {
    color: {{ section.settings.active_text_color }};
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .rb-btn.is-here--a {
    background: {{ section.settings.active_a_color }};
    border-color: {{ section.settings.active_a_color }};
  }
  .rb-btn.is-here--b {
    background: {{ section.settings.active_b_color }};
    border-color: {{ section.settings.active_b_color }};
  }
  /* hover must not undo the state */
  .rb-btn.is-here:hover { color: {{ section.settings.active_text_color }}; }
  .rb-btn.is-here--a:hover { background: {{ section.settings.active_a_color }}; filter: brightness(0.92); }
  .rb-btn.is-here--b:hover { background: {{ section.settings.active_b_color }}; filter: brightness(0.92); }

  /* The other side. `.rb-btn.is-away` is two classes, so it outranks the
     single-class fill rules (.rb-btn--moss / --cherry) in saf-rebrand.css
     without !important; the :hover pair below outranks their :hover twins the
     same way. Hover fills it in, which doubles as the affordance that it is
     still a live link. */
  .rb-btn.is-away {
    background: transparent;
    font-weight: 400;
  }
  .rb-btn.is-away--a { color: {{ section.settings.active_a_color }}; border-color: {{ section.settings.active_a_color }}; }
  .rb-btn.is-away--b { color: {{ section.settings.active_b_color }}; border-color: {{ section.settings.active_b_color }}; }
  .rb-btn.is-away--a:hover {
    background: {{ section.settings.active_a_color }};
    border-color: {{ section.settings.active_a_color }};
    color: {{ section.settings.active_text_color }};
  }
  .rb-btn.is-away--b:hover {
    background: {{ section.settings.active_b_color }};
    border-color: {{ section.settings.active_b_color }};
    color: {{ section.settings.active_text_color }};
  }
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-header__count {
    position: absolute;
    top: 4px; right: 2px;
    min-width: 17px;
    padding: 0 4px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--rb-cherry);
    color: #fff;
    font-family: var(--rb-sans);
    font-size: 11px;
    line-height: 17px;
    text-align: center;
  }

  /* Dropdowns under the path buttons. Desktop only — a phone has no hover, so
     below 750px the pills drop out of the bar entirely and the burger drawer
     plus the bottom path bar carry the navigation, as they already do. */
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-header__drop {
    position: relative;
    display: inline-flex;
  }
  /* bridges the gap between pill and panel so crossing it does not close the
     panel; explicit display because Dawn's base.css hides empty boxes */
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-header__drop::after {
    content: '';
    display: block;
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    top: 100%;
    height: 16px;
  }
  /* Card, not a menu strip: the comp draws a plain white panel floating on a
     shadow with no outline, set in the same sans at card size so the six
     destinations read as headings rather than fine print. */
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-header__drop-panel {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 5;
    top: calc(100% + 14px);
    /* 0 unless the panel would run off the right edge — see fitDropdowns() in
       saf-rebrand.js, which shifts it by exactly the overhang and no more. */
    left: var(--rb-drop-shift, 0px);
    min-width: 240px;
    max-width: calc(100vw - 32px);
    margin: 0;
    padding: 20px 26px;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 16px;
    background: {{ section.settings.background }};
    box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(30, 30, 30, 0.06), 0 14px 34px rgba(30, 30, 30, 0.13);
    list-style: none;
    opacity: 0;
    visibility: hidden;
    transform: translateY(-6px);
    transition: opacity 0.22s ease, transform 0.22s ease, visibility 0.22s;
  }
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-header__drop:hover .rb-header__drop-panel,
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-header__drop:focus-within .rb-header__drop-panel {
    opacity: 1;
    visibility: visible;
    transform: none;
  }
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-header__drop-panel a {
    display: block;
    padding: 6px 0;
    font-family: var(--rb-sans);
    font-size: var(--rb-fs-card);
    line-height: 1.35;
    color: {{ section.settings.text_color }};
    text-decoration: none;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-header__drop-panel a:hover,
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-header__drop-panel a:focus-visible {
    color: var(--rb-cherry);
  }
  /* second half of the hover corridor: the panel may be shifted left of its
     button, so the button's bridge alone does not cover a diagonal approach */
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-header__drop-panel::before {
    content: '';
    display: block;
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    bottom: 100%;
    height: 16px;
  }
  /* Fallback for the one case JS cannot cover — it has not run yet, or at all.
     Button B is the last thing before the burger, so under ~1600px a
     left-aligned panel hangs past the window edge, and a hidden panel still
     counts toward scroll width, so it would add a scrollbar even while closed. */
  @media screen and (max-width: 1580px) {
    #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-header__drop--b .rb-header__drop-panel:not(.is-fitted) {
      left: auto;
      right: 0;
    }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-header__drop-panel { transition: none; }
  }

  /* burger */
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-burger {
    display: inline-flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 7px;
    width: clamp(34px, 2.5vw, 48px);
    height: 44px;
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    background: none;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-burger span {
    display: block;
    height: 2px;
    width: 100%;
    background: {{ section.settings.text_color }};
    transition: transform 0.3s ease, opacity 0.2s ease;
  }
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-burger[aria-expanded='true'] span:nth-child(1) {
    transform: translateY(9px) rotate(45deg);
  }
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-burger[aria-expanded='true'] span:nth-child(2) { opacity: 0; }
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-burger[aria-expanded='true'] span:nth-child(3) {
    transform: translateY(-9px) rotate(-45deg);
  }

  /* Mobile path bar. Hanre's export has no mobile frames, so this keeps the
     two-path shortcut the site already had, restyled to the new brand — the
     header bar itself has no room for both pills at phone widths. */
  .rb-mobile-paths { display: none; }

  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-header__ctas { display: none; }

    {%- if section.settings.show_mobile_bar -%}
      .rb-mobile-paths {
        position: fixed;
        left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0;
        z-index: 50;
        display: flex;
        gap: 10px;
        padding: 10px 14px calc(10px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom));
        background: {{ section.settings.background }};
        border-top: 1px solid rgba(30, 30, 30, 0.12);
      }
      .rb-mobile-paths .rb-btn { flex: 1 1 0; min-width: 0; }
      body:has(.rb-mobile-paths) { padding-bottom: 78px; }
      /* keep the floating WhatsApp button clear of the bar */
      body:has(.rb-mobile-paths) .saf-whatsapp { bottom: 92px; }
    {%- endif -%}
  }
</style>

<header class="rb-section rb-header" role="banner">
  <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}" class="rb-header__logo" aria-label="{{ shop.name | escape }} — home">
    {%- if section.settings.logo != blank -%}
      {{
        section.settings.logo
        | image_url: width: 900
        | image_tag: widths: '220, 330, 440, 660, 900', alt: shop.name, loading: 'eager'
      }}
    {%- else -%}
      <img
        src="{{ 'saf-logo-lockup.png' | asset_url }}"
        alt="{{ shop.name | escape }}"
        width="330"
        height="99"
        loading="eager"
      >
    {%- endif -%}
  </a>

  <div class="rb-header__right">
    {%- comment -%}
      Instagram sits to the LEFT of the two path pills, so the run to the right
      edge reads pills → burger with nothing between them. Contact is not in the
      bar at all — it is a button in the drawer (see rb-drawer.liquid), which is
      also where the comp puts everything that is not a path pill.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if section.settings.show_instagram -%}
      {%- assign ig_url = section.settings.instagram_url | default: settings.social_instagram_link -%}
      {%- if ig_url != blank -%}
        <a href="{{ ig_url }}" class="rb-header__icon" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Instagram (opens in a new tab)">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" aria-hidden="true">
            <rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="5"></rect>
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4"></circle>
            <circle cx="17.2" cy="6.8" r="1.1" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"></circle>
          </svg>
        </a>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}

    <div class="rb-header__ctas rb-header__right">
      {%- if section.settings.cta_a_label != blank -%}
        {%- capture pill_a -%}
          <a href="{{ section.settings.cta_a_url | default: '#' }}"
             class="{{ cls_a }}"
             {% if rb_active == 'a' %}aria-current="true"{% endif %}>
            {{- section.settings.cta_a_label | escape -}}
          </a>
        {%- endcapture -%}
        {%- if has_drop_a -%}
          <div class="rb-header__drop rb-header__drop--a">
            {{ pill_a }}
            <ul class="rb-header__drop-panel">
              {%- for link in linklists[drop_a].links -%}
                <li><a href="{{ link.url }}">{{ link.title | escape }}</a></li>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
          </div>
        {%- else -%}
          {{ pill_a }}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.cta_b_label != blank -%}
        {%- capture pill_b -%}
          <a href="{{ section.settings.cta_b_url | default: '#' }}"
             class="{{ cls_b }}"
             {% if rb_active == 'b' %}aria-current="true"{% endif %}>
            {{- section.settings.cta_b_label | escape -}}
          </a>
        {%- endcapture -%}
        {%- if has_drop_b -%}
          <div class="rb-header__drop rb-header__drop--b">
            {{ pill_b }}
            <ul class="rb-header__drop-panel">
              {%- for link in linklists[drop_b].links -%}
                <li><a href="{{ link.url }}">{{ link.title | escape }}</a></li>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
          </div>
        {%- else -%}
          {{ pill_b }}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- if section.settings.show_search -%}
      <a href="{{ routes.search_url }}" class="rb-header__icon" aria-label="Search">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" aria-hidden="true">
          <circle cx="11" cy="11" r="7"></circle><path d="M20 20l-3.5-3.5"></path>
        </svg>
      </a>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if section.settings.show_cart -%}
      <a href="{{ routes.cart_url }}" class="rb-header__icon" aria-label="Cart ({{ cart.item_count }})">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M6 8h12l-1 12H7L6 8z"></path><path d="M9 8V6a3 3 0 0 1 6 0v2"></path>
        </svg>
        {%- if cart.item_count > 0 -%}
          <span class="rb-header__count">{{ cart.item_count }}</span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </a>
    {%- endif -%}

    <button
      type="button"
      class="rb-burger"
      aria-expanded="false"
      aria-controls="rb-drawer-{{ sid }}"
      aria-label="Open menu"
      data-rb-drawer-open
    >
      <span></span><span></span><span></span>
    </button>
  </div>
</header>

{%- if section.settings.show_mobile_bar -%}
  {%- if section.settings.cta_a_label != blank or section.settings.cta_b_label != blank -%}
    <nav class="rb-mobile-paths" aria-label="Browse by path">
      {%- comment -%}
        Same fills as the desktop pills. The header pills are hidden at this
        width, so this bar IS the two-path control on a phone — leaving it
        outline while the desktop pair is coloured would read as two different
        designs on one site.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if section.settings.cta_a_label != blank -%}
        <a href="{{ section.settings.cta_a_url | default: '#' }}"
           class="{{ cls_a }}"
           {% if rb_active == 'a' %}aria-current="true"{% endif %}>
          {{- section.settings.cta_a_label | escape -}}
        </a>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if section.settings.cta_b_label != blank -%}
        <a href="{{ section.settings.cta_b_url | default: '#' }}"
           class="{{ cls_b }}"
           {% if rb_active == 'b' %}aria-current="true"{% endif %}>
          {{- section.settings.cta_b_label | escape -}}
        </a>
      {%- endif -%}
    </nav>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- render 'rb-drawer', sid: sid, menu: menu, section: section, active: rb_active -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Rebrand header",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "rb-header-section",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "logo", "label": "Logo",
      "info": "Leave blank to use the supplied SA Art Fair lockup." },
    { "type": "range", "id": "logo_width", "min": 140, "max": 420, "step": 5,
      "default": 275, "unit": "px", "label": "Logo width" },
    { "type": "link_list", "id": "menu", "default": "main-menu", "label": "Drawer menu" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "sticky", "default": true, "label": "Stick to top on scroll" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_border", "default": false, "label": "Show bottom border" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Path buttons" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cta_a_label", "default": "Buy Art", "label": "Button A label" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "cta_a_url", "label": "Button A link" },
    { "type": "select", "id": "cta_a_fill", "label": "Button A style", "default": "outline",
      "info": "Outline is the design as drawn. The colours are the Store and Studio halves of the palette.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "outline", "label": "Outline (as designed)" },
        { "value": "cherry", "label": "Cherry" },
        { "value": "moss", "label": "Moss" },
        { "value": "teal", "label": "Teal" },
        { "value": "sage-solid", "label": "Sage" }
      ] },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cta_b_label", "default": "Make Art", "label": "Button B label" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "cta_b_url", "label": "Button B link" },
    { "type": "select", "id": "cta_b_fill", "label": "Button B style", "default": "outline",
      "options": [
        { "value": "outline", "label": "Outline (as designed)" },
        { "value": "cherry", "label": "Cherry" },
        { "value": "moss", "label": "Moss" },
        { "value": "teal", "label": "Teal" },
        { "value": "sage-solid", "label": "Sage" }
      ] },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "enable_dropdowns", "default": false,
      "label": "Open a dropdown under each button",
      "info": "Desktop only — phones have no hover, so there the two pills and the burger are unchanged. Add one 'Button dropdown' block per button and pick its menu. The buttons stay clickable links either way." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_mobile_bar", "default": true,
      "label": "Show path bar on mobile",
      "info": "The pills do not fit the header bar on phones. Not part of the desktop design — the Figma has no mobile frames." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Highlight the section you are in" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "highlight_active", "default": true,
      "label": "Fill the button for the side you are on",
      "info": "Buy Art fills while you are anywhere in the Store, Make Art while you are anywhere in the Studio. Classes, workshops and teacher pages resolve on their own from the product type; the lists below only cover pages that hold no products." },
    { "type": "color", "id": "active_a_color", "default": "#505a43", "label": "Button A highlight" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "active_b_color", "default": "#e07468", "label": "Button B highlight" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "active_text_color", "default": "#ffffff", "label": "Highlight text" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "cta_a_paths", "label": "Extra paths that count as Button A",
      "default": "/pages/collect-art, /pages/artists, /collections/gallery, /collections/wishlist, /collections/warm-tones, /collections/cool-tones, /collections/neutral-tones",
      "info": "Comma separated. A partial match counts, so /collections/artist- covers every artist page." },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "cta_b_paths", "label": "Extra paths that count as Button B",
      "default": "/pages/create-art, /pages/studio, /pages/the-team, /pages/term-4, /pages/classes-workshops, /collections/classes, /collections/workshops, /collections/teachers" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Icons",
      "info": "Instagram sits to the LEFT of the two path buttons, so nothing separates them from the menu button. The design shows no search or cart in the bar; the drawer carries the cart link instead." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_instagram", "default": true, "label": "Show Instagram button",
      "info": "Shows it in the bar and beside the call button in the slide-in menu." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "instagram_url", "label": "Instagram URL",
      "info": "Leave blank to use the store's Instagram link from Theme settings → Social media." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_search", "default": false, "label": "Show search icon" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_cart", "default": false, "label": "Show cart icon" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Drawer" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_contact", "default": true, "label": "Show call button in the menu",
      "info": "A phone icon on the row above the two path buttons, next to Instagram. Instagram uses the switch under Icons above." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "phone_number", "label": "Phone number",
      "info": "Dialled by the call button, e.g. +27 72 477 8807. Leave blank to use the WhatsApp number from Theme settings; with no number anywhere the button opens the contact page instead." },
